18/09\n[0]Volunteering and Leadership:\n[1]Role: Committee Student Member\n[1]Organization: Scholarship Committee at the Faculty of Engineering, University of Toronto\n[1]Location: Toronto, ON, Canada\n[1]Duration: 2020/01 - 2020/12\n[1]Description: Collaborated as part of a multi-disciplinary committee, providing impactful decisions to benefit students faculty-wide. Represented students by distributing and voting on awards and scholarships for students\n[0]Work Experience:\n[1]Job Title: Freelance 3D Designer\n[1]Company: Freelance\n[1]Location: Toronto, ON, Canada\n[1]Duration: 2024/01 - 2024/09\n[1]Description: Designed quality models for 3D printed products, applying technical skills in Blender and various slicing software/hardware. Utilized problem-solving expertise to create innovative designs\n[1]Job Title: PEY VR Technical Assistant\n[1]Company: Medica Providencia Clinic\n[1]Location: Tuxtla Gtz, CS, Mexico\n[1]Duration: 2022/12 - 2023/03\n[1]Description: Utilized problem-solving skills to troubleshoot hardware issues, improving efficiency and patient satisfaction. Collaborated with professionals on testing processes\n[1]Job Title: Script Programmer and Video Project Editor\n[1]Company: Ontario Institute for Studies in Education\n[1]Location: Toronto, ON, Canada\n[1]Duration: 2022/03 - 2022/05\n[1]Description: Developed video description generation algorithms using Python, enhancing stakeholder satisfaction and project deliverables within 3 months. Utilized creative problem-solving skills to align project goals\n[1]Job Title: Secretary and Sales Associate\n[1]Company: Medica Providencia Clinic\n[1]Location: Tuxtla Gtz, CS, Mexico\n[1]Duration: 2015/08 - 2018/07\n[1]Description: Streamlined operations by efficiently managing tasks, demonstrating skills in data entry and documentation, and performing sales operations. This experience showcases my ability to manage peak hours and adapt to changing demands\n[0]Projects:\n[1]Project Title: TTRPG Tools\n[1]URL: https://github.com/Marneus981/TTRPGTools\n[1]Type: Open Source Personal Project\n[1]Duration: 2023/06 - Present\n[1]Description: Developed software tools with planned AI integration for playing and creating TTRPG Games using C++ and Python, highlighting skills in programming languages, automation, and debugging\n[1]Project Title: VKnob\n[1]URL: https://github.com/Marneus981/VKnob\n[1]Type: Open Source Personal Project\n[1]Duration: 2024/02 - Present\n[1]Description: Developed an overlay application controlling multiple Digital Audio Workstations, showcasing proficiency in C++ and UIAutomation. Demonstrated ability to automate UI calls in Windows\n[1]Project Title: Untitled RPG Game Project\n[1]URL: \n[1]Type: Personal Game Project\n[1]Duration: 2025/04 - Present\n[1]Description: Developed a 2D action role-playing game using Unity, showcasing C# programming skills and editing/animating 2D sprites and assets\n[1]Project Title: Horizontal Federated Learning Research\n[1]URL: github.com/alexjsenn/FedScale\n[1]Type: Research | Capstone Project\n[1]Duration: 2021/09 - 2022/06\n[1]Description: Developed Python skills, researched network performance of distributed Federated Machine Learning model aggregation, and improved algorithm efficiency. Co-authored technical papers on novel aggregation algorithms\n[1]Project Title: MAPPA C++ Geographical Information System\n[1]URL: https://github.com/Marneus981/MAPPA\n[1]Type: University Project\n[1]Duration: 2019/09 - 2020/06\n[1]Description: Built a GIS system using OpenStreetMap data and C++ EZGL library, improving efficiency by 200% and reducing memory usage by 50%. Co-developed UI/UX tailored to stakeholder needs\n[0]Skills:\n[1]Programming Languages: Programming Languages\n[1]Technical Skills: 3D Printing, 3D modelling, Algorithm optimization, Automated Testing, Back-End Development, Blender, Data Entry, Distributed Systems, Federated Machine Learning, JavaScript, Machine Learning, Microsoft Suite, Object-oriented design principles, Product Design, Project Management, Python, Scripting, Slicing Software, Software Development, Unit Testing, Unit testing, Unity, Version Control with Git, Version control, Version control systems\n[1]Soft Skills: Collaboration, Communication, Detail-Oriented, Effective communication, Fast Learning, Good Written and Communication Skills, Integrity, Self-Starter, Teamwork, Time Management", 'job_description': 'Here is the summary:\n\n**Company Name:** Sentry\n**Job Title:** Software Engineer, New Grad\n\n**Key Responsibilities:**\n\n* Develop and extend the Sentry product by writing software in either Python or JavaScript (or both)\n* Participate in the full software development lifecycle - design, development, testing, and operating in production\n* Communicate effectively with team members, other teams, and stakeholders (product managers)\n\n**Required Skills:**\n\n* B.S. or higher in Computer Science (or similar degree program)\n* At least 1 previous internship or equivalent practical experience\n* Implementation skills with one or more general-purpose programming languages (e.g., Python, JavaScript, Java, etc.)\n* Good knowledge of:\n\t+ Algorithms\n\t+ Data structures\n\t+ Object-oriented design principles\n* Experience working with:\n\t+ Version control\n\t+ Unit testing\n\n**Soft Skills:**\n\n* Act on feedback, coaching, and mentorship from manager and teammates\n* Demonstrate a passion for actively using the product being built (Sentry)\n\n**Desired Qualities:**\n\n* Interest in contributing to an open-source project daily\n* Excitement about joining a high-growth startup and modern software development team that iterates & ships code rapidly.', 'standard_calls': ['make_cover_letter_text'], 'non_standard_calls': []}
